":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.03405138380112005,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":7.4,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.12640620314851556,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.12727,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":84.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.071,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":7.1,"pf":[],"description_full":"Upstart Holdings, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, operates a cloud-based artificial intelligence (AI) lending platform in the United States. The company operates through three segments: Personal Lending, Auto Lending, and Other. Its platform includes unsecured personal loans, small dollar loans, auto refinance, auto retail loans, and auto secured personal loan, and home equity lines of credit. Upstart Holdings, Inc. was founded in 2012 and is headquartered in San Mateo, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Paul  Gu | CEO & Director | Age 34 | Compensation: $894,920 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $743K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $94K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Upstart Holdings, Inc. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $2.2B market cap on $1.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +7% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 1% against a 13% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $148M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 1.0\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 13% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 13% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.2\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (31.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 25% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 178% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.779902940336854},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +6.8% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (93% sell ratio, net $3.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-we